  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1. All completed experiments use concat fusion; we have zero data on weighted fusion. The key uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) meaningfully affects how the RNA and image signals combine, which is a fundamental architectural choice. Question: config_019 is identical to config_018 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, giving a clean single-variable A/B test that isolates the fusion effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) Fusion is a completely untested design axis, so any result reduces uncertainty on a core decision. (2) The answer generalizes across all future multimodal configurations—if weighted fusion helps, we adopt it everywhere; if not, we confirm concat suffices and can pivot to RNA encoder or image encoder exploration. (3) It is the most budget-efficient choice: one experiment resolves a binary architectural question with no confounds, rather than testing a new RNA encoder (e.g., scvi) which, while also informative, is a second-order question relative to how the two modalities are combined."
}

